  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="171">
    <Text UId="172"> NOT #stationDown is the important half of this guard. When a station is off the network</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="173" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="174" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="175">
    <Text UId="176"> its input data is not a report from the field, and what the process image holds instead</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="177" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="178" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="179">
    <Text UId="180"> is not something this project has been able to establish - Siemens' own documentation</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="181" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="182" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="183">
    <Text UId="184"> was not found to say whether inputs go to zero or freeze at their last value, and it</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="185" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="186" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="187">
    <Text UId="188"> cannot be tested in simulation because PLCSIM runs no PROFINET. Both possibilities are</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="189" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="190" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="191">
    <Text UId="192"> bad in different ways: zeros make every valve on the station report no position and not</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="193" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="194" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="195">
    <Text UId="196"> healthy, which is ~54 alarms burying the one that explains them; frozen values make a</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="197" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="198" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="199">
    <Text UId="200"> dead station look perfectly normal.</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="201" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="202" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="203">
    <Text UId="204" />
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="205" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="206" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="207">
    <Text UId="208"> Skipping the copy removes the question. Valve[i].OpenFB/ClosedFB/Healthy/LocalMode</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="209" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="210" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="211">
    <Text UId="212"> simply keep the values they last had, which is the last real report from the field -</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="213" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="214" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="215">
    <Text UId="216"> the thing an operator actually needs when a station drops, since knowing whether a</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="217" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="218" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="219">
    <Text UId="220"> ballast line was open or shut is the first question asked. And because Healthy stays</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="221" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="222" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="223">
    <Text UId="224"> TRUE and the position stays valid, the Unhealthy and Loss-of-Position alarms do not</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="225" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="226" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="227">
    <Text UId="228"> fire for the whole station, leaving the RIO station alarm standing on its own.</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="229" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="230" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="231">
    <Text UId="232" />
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="233" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="234" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="235">
    <Text UId="236"> Travel timeouts are deliberately NOT suppressed. If someone commands a valve on a dead</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="237" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="238" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="239">
    <Text UId="240"> station, nothing moves and FailOpen/FailClose is the correct thing to say - that is one</Text>
  </LineComment>
  <NewLine Num="1" UId="241" />
  <Blank Num="8" UId="242" />
  <LineComment Inserted="false" NoClosingBracket="false" UId="243">
    <Text UId="244"> alarm about one deliberate action, not a flood.</Text>
